    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1988-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(b=2a\\) and \\(c=3b=6a.\\) Therefore \\(\\frac{a+b}{b+c}=\\frac{3a}{8a}=\\frac38.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write both \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) as multiples of \\(a\\)",
        "Substitute those expressions into \\(\\frac{a+b}{b+c}\\)"
      ],
